# Waygr

Before starting any task, read `/docs` in this order:

1. **`docs/BUILD-BRIEF.md`** — source of truth. If anything conflicts, BUILD wins.
2. `docs/architecture.md` · `docs/patterns-brief.md` · `docs/prd.md`
3. `docs/BRAND-BRIEF.md` · `docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md` · `docs/GROWTH-LOOP.md`

## Locked decisions

- Next.js **15** App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, Serwist, Vercel
- Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Realtime, Storage, Edge Functions, Cron) + Drizzle migrations
- **Forfeits** — drinks, food, honor-system money OK; no payment rails, prizes, or escrow
- **21+** age gate (not 18)
- First signed-in non-creator takes the other side; lock at kickoff
- Leagues: NFL, NCAAF, NBA (NCAAB before March)
- Score feed only; `ScoreProvider` interface; BALLDONTLIE first
- `APP_NAME` in `lib/constants.ts`; every UI string in `lib/copy.ts`
- Brand tokens in `styles/tokens.css` + `lib/theme.ts`; dark default

## Non-goals (Phase 1)

- Payment rails (Stripe, Venmo/Apple Pay linking, wallets, escrow) — honor money on the line is OK
- Prizes or sportsbook odds
- Stranger matching or public challenge feed
- Groups, rooms, leaderboards, counter-offers (Phase 2)
- Native app, iMessage, Live Activities, widgets (Phase 3)
- Importing contacts; Waygr sending texts or emails
- Chat outside a challenge

## Color and voice rules

- Colors **only** from brand tokens — no off-palette hex in app source
- Text on orange is always ink (`--on-accent`), never white
- Orange = you / primary action (one per screen). Blue = their side only
- No red for losing; rose is errors only
- Shipping UI noun = **waygr** (Chris 2026-09-24); prefer waygr + forfeit. Call/challenge OK in casual speech. Never bet, wager, odds, or payout in UI copy

## Chris-only parks (do not block on these)

- Challenge link domain
- Apple Developer account
- BALLDONTLIE tier after confirming live + period scores for NFL and NCAAF
